<title>UK: Rover recalls 23,000 vehicles - PA.</title>
<headline>Rover recalls 23,000 vehicles - PA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rover Group, the UK motor manufacturer owned by Germany's BMW, has recalled 23,000 Land Rover Discovery vehicles because of a a fault in the driver's door, according to a report on the PA news agency on Friday.</p>
<p>The report said a faulty latch had been found on the driver's front door of some of the Discoveries and that the recall involves models built between April 1995 and July 1995. No-one at Rover was available to comment on the story.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
